@SecureVault.Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7091
@accessToken = ENTER_YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@refreshToken = ENTER_YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE

# ##########################################################################
# SecureVault.Api.http — Manual API Testing File
#
# This file is used to manually test the SecureVault API endpoints directly
# from your IDE (Rider, Visual Studio, or VS Code with the REST Client
# extension). Each "###" separator defines an individual request that you
# can execute independently by clicking the green ▶ play button next to it.
#
# HOW TO USE
# ----------
# 1. Start the API first:
#        cd SecureVault.Api
#        dotnet run --launch-profile https
#
# 2. Update the variables below before sending requests:
#    • SecureVault.Api_HostAddress — Base URL of the running API.
#      Change it only if you modified the port in launchSettings.json.
#    • accessToken — A valid JWT. To obtain one, execute the
#      "Login as SuperAdmin" request below, then copy the "accessToken"
#      value from the response body and paste it here.
#    • refreshToken — A valid refresh token. Copy the "refreshToken"
#      value from any login response and paste it here.
#
#    Variables are referenced in requests as {{variableName}}.
#
# NOTES
# -----
# • Tokens expire quickly (default: 3 min). Re-login and update
#   the accessToken variable whenever you get a 401 Unauthorized response.
# • Usernames are unique — if a registration returns a conflict error,
#   choose a different username or delete the SQLite database and restart.
# ##########################################################################

## Register a new user without role, should fail.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testGuestUser",
  "password": "testGuest@1234"  
}

### Register a new Guest user
### Should pass unless the username is taken.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testGuestUser",
  "password": "testGuest@1234",
  "role": "Guest"
}

### Test login with new Guest user created.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testGuestUser",
  "password": "testGuest@1234"
}


### Register a user with User role
### Should pass, unless the username is taken.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testUser",
  "password": "testUser@1234",
  "role": "User"
}

### Test new User user created.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testUser",
  "password": "testUser@1234"
}


### Login as SuperAdmin
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "superadmin",
  "password": "superAdmin123_!!"
}

### Register an admin user.
### Should pass if there's a user with SuperAdmin Role logged in and the new username is not taken.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/register-admin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "userName": "testAdminUser",
  "password": "testAdmin@1234",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### Test new Admin user created.
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testAdminUser",
  "password": "testAdmin@1234"
}

### Test refresh token to get a new access token
POST {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "RefreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Get claims from token on a readble format
GET {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### This endpoint only requires to be authenticated with any role
GET {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### This endpoint requires to have an Admin or SuperAdmin role
### Should return forbidden otherwise
GET {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/admin-role
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### This endpoint is allowed for any role except Guest
### Should return forbidden if the token belongs to a Guest user.
GET {{SecureVault.Api_HostAddress}}/no-guests
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}